Subject: Nightingale Update - Priority One

Agent Kepler,

Received your comm regarding the Zurich rendezvous. Good work securing the initial contact, though the subject, Herr Vogel, proved more…resistant than anticipated. His security detail is tighter than the reports indicated – a private firm specializing in ex-Spetsnaz, apparently. We need to recalibrate our threat assessment.

The package he possesses – designated ‘Nightingale’ – is confirmed to be a fully functional prototype of the sonic disruptor. Not the scaled-down version we initially believed. This changes everything. Its range and potential for collateral damage are significantly higher. Retrieval is now absolutely critical, not just desirable.

I’ve reviewed the surveillance footage you transmitted. Vogel is exhibiting erratic behavior – increased paranoia, frequent changes in routine, and a noticeable reliance on a specific brand of chamomile tea – a detail that might seem insignificant, but could indicate a method for calming his nerves, or even a delivery mechanism for something else. Investigate the tea source. Trace it back to the distributor, then to the origin. 

The secondary contact, Frau Schmidt, remains clean, but maintain observation. She’s a known associate of several individuals with ties to ‘The Serpent’s Coil’ – a shadow organization we’ve been tracking for years. It’s possible Vogel is acting on their orders, or that they’re interested in Nightingale as well.

Regarding extraction, the original plan is compromised. The safe house is under increased surveillance – likely Vogel’s team. We need a new location, preferably one with multiple escape routes and minimal civilian presence. I’m forwarding coordinates for a disused observatory on the outskirts of the city. It’s dilapidated, but offers a clear line of sight and several underground tunnels.

Be extremely cautious. Vogel is not a fool, and he’s clearly aware he’s being watched. Avoid direct confrontation if possible. Prioritize securing Nightingale. If capture is unavoidable, activate the failsafe – the dental implant. It’s a last resort, but preferable to the device falling into the wrong hands. 

I’m dispatching Agent Rhys as backup. He’ll arrive in Zurich within 24 hours, posing as a journalist. He’s proficient in close-quarters combat and has experience with sonic weaponry. Coordinate with him upon his arrival. 

Remember the stakes, Kepler. Nightingale in the wrong hands could destabilize entire regions. This is not just a retrieval mission; it’s a containment operation. 

Maintain radio silence unless absolutely necessary. Use the encrypted channel only for critical updates. 

Over and out.

Director Thorne.



